{
  "mn68:0.1": "Middle Discourses 68 ",
  "mn68:0.2": "At Naḷakapāna ",
  "mn68:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn68:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Kosalans near Naḷakapāna in the grove of flame-of-the-forest trees. ",
  "mn68:2.1": "Now at that time several very well-known gentlemen had gone forth out of faith from the lay life to homelessness in the Buddha’s name—",
  "mn68:2.2": "The venerables Anuruddha, Bhaddiya, Kimbila, Bhagu, Kuṇḍadhāna, Revata, Ānanda, and other very well-known gentlemen. ",
  "mn68:3.1": "Now at that time the Buddha was sitting in the open, surrounded by the mendicant Saṅgha. ",
  "mn68:3.2": "Then the Buddha spoke to the mendicants about those gentlemen: ",
  "mn68:3.3": "“Mendicants, those gentlemen who have gone forth out of faith from the lay life to homelessness in my name—I trust they’re satisfied with the spiritual life?” ",
  "mn68:3.4": "When this was said, the mendicants kept silent. ",
  "mn68:3.5": "For a second and a third time the Buddha asked the same question. ",
  "mn68:3.6": "",
  "mn68:3.7": "",
  "mn68:3.8": "",
  "mn68:3.9": "",
  "mn68:3.10": "For a third time, the mendicants kept silent. ",
  "mn68:4.1": "Then it occurred to the Buddha, ",
  "mn68:4.2": "“Why don’t I question just those gentlemen?” ",
  "mn68:4.3": "Then the Buddha said to Venerable Anuruddha, ",
  "mn68:4.4": "“Anuruddha and friends, I hope you’re satisfied with the spiritual life?” ",
  "mn68:4.5": "“Indeed, sir, we are satis